## [Getting started](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/getting-started.md)

- [Create an Amazon Kinesis video stream](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/gs-createstream.md): Use the Amazon Kinesis Video Streams console or AWS CLI to create your first Kinesis video stream.
- [Send data to an Amazon Kinesis video stream](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/gs-send-data.md): This section describes how to send media data from a camera to the Kinesis video stream that you created in the previous section.
- [Consume media data](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/gs-consume-data.md): You can consume media data by either viewing it in the console, or by creating an application that reads media data from a stream using Hypertext Live Streaming (HLS).


